WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.081 --> 00:00:02.855
Skyler Bouchard: The State
Fair of Texas sells over

00:00:02.855 --> 00:00:05.180
half a million corn dogs per year.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.727
That's because they claim to have sold

00:00:06.727 --> 00:00:10.280
the first corn dog ever back in 1942.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.810
Everyone in Texas will
tell you that the corny dog

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.610
is the most delicious
corn dog they've ever had.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.820
Today, I'm gonna try the OG corny dog,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.480
along with some
traditional saltwater taffy

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.020
and a funnel cake bacon cheeseburger

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.250
to tell you which is my favorite.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.950
The winner might surprise you.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.033
Let's dig in.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.400
I'm Skyler Bouchard.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.130
For the past eight years,
I've been traveling the world

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.130
and learning about different cuisines.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.800
I've taken everything I've
learned to my kitchen,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.220
and now I'm on the hunt

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.720
for the best festival and
fair foods in North America.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.010
Today, I'm at the State Fair of Texas,

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:49.400
the longest-running fair
in the entire country.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.807
The State Fair of Texas

00:00:50.807 --> 00:00:52.881
is the biggest state fair in America,

00:00:52.881 --> 00:00:55.550
with over 2 million people
attending each fall.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:56.953
They also offer more food

00:00:56.953 --> 00:00:59.470
than almost any state fair in the country.

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.930
Karissa Condoianis: The State
Fair of Texas was founded

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.610
in 1886 as a livestock exposition.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:06.383
We have hundreds of
concessionaires out here

00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:09.020
with thousands of food
items on their menus.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.610
Even if you're not from
here, you know, as they say,

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.980
I may not have been born in Texas,

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.100
but I got here as quick as I could.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.080
Skyler: I tried everything
from fried butter

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.770
to fried peanut butter and jelly,

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:22.540
but I narrowed it down to
three final contenders.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.560
One of the reasons the State
Fair of Texas is so famous

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.000
is because it debuted
one of the most important

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.820
fair foods of all time: the corn dog.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.530
In 1938, brothers Neil and Carl Fletcher

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.400
claimed to have invented the corn dog,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.380
which they called the corny dog.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:40.240
That year, the idea of a
hot dog covered in corn

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.510
and deep-fried was so unheard of

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.285
that they had to walk around the fair

00:01:44.285 --> 00:01:45.835
giving them away for free

00:01:45.835 --> 00:01:47.910
in order to get people to try them.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:50.135
Aaron Fletcher: First year they sold

00:01:50.135 --> 00:01:51.820
a couple hundred of them,

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.760
once they finally got people to try them.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.110
And now we sell about anywhere between

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.726
500,000 and 600,000 corny dogs a year.

00:01:59.726 --> 00:02:03.070
We go through about
1,600 gallons of mustard.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.210
About 800 gallons of ketchup.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.800
I've heard people say that
they've waited up to an hour,

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.430
hour and a half, back in the line.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.327
We got generations that come out here

00:02:13.327 --> 00:02:14.768
year after year after year after year.

00:02:26.053 --> 00:02:30.060
Customer: They're actually hand
dipped in cornbread batter.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.410
And I know, it's a Southern
thing, it's delicious.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.700
There's none other that tastes like this.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:35.750
Customer: They're the best.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.620
They're crunchy, good, always hot.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.980
They just taste better than any corn dog

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.460
you're gonna get anywhere else.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.008
Skyler: I grew up eating
corn dogs all the time,

00:02:44.008 --> 00:02:48.292
so I'm really excited to try
the one and only corny dog.

00:02:51.989 --> 00:02:53.114
Mm.

00:02:53.114 --> 00:02:57.130
All right, there's a lot
of flavor happening here,

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.375
and it's not as sweet as

00:02:58.375 --> 00:03:00.136
the other corn dogs I've had before.

00:03:00.136 --> 00:03:03.110
The hot dog is smoky and savory.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.290
All in all, this is a winner.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.590
I can definitely see why
people would wait hours

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:08.940
for this corn dog.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.570
While this corn dog was delicious,

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.882
I'll be interested to see
if it's really my favorite

00:03:12.882 --> 00:03:14.300
since it's so simple.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.080
And I have two other
unique contenders to try.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.721
Time to see how the hidden gem compares.

00:03:21.216 --> 00:03:24.080
Sutter's Taffy started back in 1919,

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.960
and they still use old-fashioned
methods and machines

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.930
to make their delicious saltwater taffy.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.640
Ed Sutter founded Sutter's Taffy

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.470
after working at an
amusement park as a kid.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:35.923
He saw the taffy pullers there

00:03:35.923 --> 00:03:39.540
making small pieces of taffy,
which they called kisses.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.780
And then he bought his
own taffy-pulling machines

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.484
and went on the road.

00:03:43.484 --> 00:03:46.320
Sutter's Taffy quickly
became extremely successful,

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.820
selling over 1 million boxes of taffy

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.080
at the 1939 World's Fair.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.160
Tony King and his family
bought the business

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.650
from Sutter's granddaughter in 2008,

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.210
but they still use the same methods

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.740
that Sutter did back then.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:02.770
Tony King: So, we bring in
660-pound barrels of corn syrup,

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:05.080
and so we batch each pot
with corn syrup, sugar,

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.430
and butter, and then we
put it on our taffy pullers

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.570
to aerate it, and that's
where we flavor it.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:10.851
At the State Fair of Texas,

00:04:10.851 --> 00:04:13.108
we will make over a million kisses.

00:04:13.108 --> 00:04:14.520
Skyler: So, I go in like this?

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.526
Tony: Yep, pull it straight down.

00:04:15.526 --> 00:04:16.733
Skyler: Pull it down,

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.780
and whew!

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:19.613
Tony: It's fresh.

00:04:19.613 --> 00:04:20.880
We make candy every day right here

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.497
on the State Fair grounds.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.034
This is the candy you made.

00:04:25.034 --> 00:04:26.278
Skyler: That we just made?
Tony: Just made.

00:04:26.278 --> 00:04:27.369
Skyler: Oh, my gosh!

00:04:27.369 --> 00:04:28.759
All right, I have to try one.

00:04:28.759 --> 00:04:30.939
We just made these. This
is the peanut butter?

00:04:30.939 --> 00:04:32.264
Tony: Yep, peanut butter.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.333
Perfect.

00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:39.376
Skyler: It's so sticky and smushy.

00:04:39.376 --> 00:04:40.659
Tony: Yep, salty and sweet.

00:04:40.659 --> 00:04:43.221
Skyler: Salty, sweet, creamy, delicious.

00:04:43.221 --> 00:04:46.380
It's like peanut butter
and marshmallow spread.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:47.402
Tony: Yeah, it's great.

00:04:47.402 --> 00:04:48.235
Skyler: Mm-hmm.

00:04:48.235 --> 00:04:50.000
Finally, I'm heading to a fair stand

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.020
that's known for its
bizarre flavor combos.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.630
Time to see which will
take the final crown,

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:59.384
the classic corny dog,
simple saltwater taffy,

00:04:59.384 --> 00:05:01.711
or our wacky snack.

00:05:02.752 --> 00:05:05.200
The wackiest snack at
the State Fair of Texas

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.110
is the funnel cake bacon queso burger,

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.690
which won the Most Creative Big Tex Award

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:14.430
and the Best Savory
Dish Award back in 2017.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.550
This burger is an
estimated 2,100 calories.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.790
I got in the kitchen to see how it's made.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.940
Tom Grace: Are you ready to make it?

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.525
Skyler: I am ready to make
a funnel cake queso burger!

00:05:24.525 --> 00:05:25.490
With bacon!
Tom: Let's do it.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:28.070
Every year, we're looking
for the most fantastic,

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:31.380
outrageous thing we can
find to put out there

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.410
that will make fairgoers say, "Wow."

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:36.850
Little funnel cakes,
awesome grilled burger,

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:37.980
crispy strips of bacon,

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.860
and then some really hot queso sauce.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:43.080
So, the simplicity of it is
what works so well together.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.771
Here we go.

00:05:44.771 --> 00:05:45.890
[Skyler cheering]

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.010
Now the only other thing
we need is our little knife

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.560
that holds it all together.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.393
Do you want to?

00:05:50.393 --> 00:05:51.226
Skyler: Stab it in the center?

00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:52.270
Tom: Yeah, right down the middle.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:53.148
Skyler: All right, ready?

00:05:53.148 --> 00:05:54.322
Tom: Yeah, push it.
Skyler: There you go.

00:05:54.322 --> 00:05:55.155
Tom: Oh, you did it.

00:05:55.155 --> 00:05:58.240
Skyler: Yeah, nice work! That was awesome.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.257
Let's see here. OK.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:08.720
All right, some thoughts.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.670
The funnel cake is crispy and sweet.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:14.180
It's char-grilled,
smoky, delicious burger.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.870
The bacon adds that fat, which is flavor.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.060
Everybody loves a waterfall of cheese.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.770
This all came together so well.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.267
Honestly, I always get skeptical

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:27.430
of those sweet and savory burgers.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:29.860
This is better than I thought it would be.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.570
And it had way more flavor
than I thought it would have.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:36.511
It really is a
once-in-a-lifetime experience.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.400
It's really a competition
between the old and the new.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.550
We had the first-ever corny dog,

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.300
Sutter's historic saltwater taffy,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.213
and then this new fusion of
the funnel cake queso burger.

00:06:52.213 --> 00:06:54.710
But I have to say my favorite one

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:58.130
was the funnel cake bacon queso burger.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:59.920
I love saying that.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.397
You know, you come to these fairs,

00:07:01.397 --> 00:07:04.090
and you want to eat foods
that are an experience,

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.760
and it was really just that.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.385
It had so much going on,

00:07:07.385 --> 00:07:09.868
and obviously it had some fried food,

00:07:09.868 --> 00:07:13.450
some meat, some cheese, things I love.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.280
I loved getting behind the counter

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.023
and learning how it was made,

00:07:17.023 --> 00:07:19.044
and eating it was truly an experience

00:07:19.044 --> 00:07:22.220
that you could only get at
the State Fair of Texas.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:23.343
We'll see you next time.

00:07:23.343 --> 00:07:24.296
Stay hungry.

